  "details": "[Updated old post, as I didn't understand this 'bug' prior]\n\nThis is an issue in many worlds that makes use of UI inputfields. (Karaoke central being a common example)\n\nAt seemingly random, keyboard movement will suddenly start typing into inputfields. I assume this functionality even exists because VRChat once didn't have the popup for a keyboard in desktop. However, VRChat now uses a keyboard popup specifically for inputfields, and navigation is almost never left on intentionally for worlds. Leaving this as something that worsens the quality of maps from newer creators without them understanding why.\n\nI'm not sure if the 'navigation' is bugged, or if this is some \"feature\" that isn't documented and is on by default. But considering the inconsistency of it's activation, and the QoL it would be if it were outright removed, I assume it's a bug.",
